Hello,
I am trying my hand at embedding R in Java, so following the JNI pdf I
successfully managed to emebed the R engine and parse and eval
strings.
I know JRI does this already but I want a minimal embedding, where
only one Java thread will call the native functions to just parse and
eval strings (no assignment nor reading back).

However, I repeatedly suffer a segfaul whenever R encounters and error
e.g my Java call is

evalR("1(2)");

and the output is
Error: attempt to apply non-function
Invalid memory access of location 0x0 rip=0x0

(on RHEL 64 it is similar).
I can call evalR("stop('ss')");
and get the same segfault.

I was wondering if anyone has an idea why the crash?
I have kept relevant source here  http://www.stat.purdue.edu/~sguha/jni/html/

Thank you
Saptarshi

