With this final code:

>     REXP environment = engine.newEnvironment(null, false);
>     //... do some work with the environment ...
>     //Clean environment
>     engine.assign("myenv",environment);
>     engine.parseAndEval("rm(list=ls(envir=myenv), envir=myenv)", null, false); //(null=global environment)

and also removing the environment at the end of each iteration:

 >     engine.parseAndEval("rm(list=\"myenv\")", null, false);

we fixed this issue.

Applying a similar patch also resolved the problem in our production 
code (no more jvm crashes).
Probably in R there is a memory leak with the maximum number of 
variable/environment we can crate (we checked the total memory used 
during each run, and was always small).

It's also a little bit tricky creating the environment through API and 
managing it through R code, should be very useful having some method 
like "engine.removeEnvironment(...", etc.

Thank you.
Regards,
Fabio



