Subject: Creating database table with lower case names using RJDBC
Message-ID: <971536df1001140800h6472d002hade00f5b8af9d0bf@mail.gmail.com>

I am using the H2 database (http://www.h2database.com) with RJDBC and
if I use a create statement I can create a table with lower case
column names but not if I use dbWriteTable.  The code below
illustrates this.

The problem is likely that the create statement that dbWriteTable is
generating does not quote the column names as the explicit create
statement shown below does.

First we show how to do it with an explicit create statement (it
works) and then we try it with dbWriteTable (it does not work -- it
creates upper case names rather than the case asked for).

> library(RJDBC)
> drv <- JDBC("org.h2.Driver", "C:\\Program Files\\H2\\bin\\h2.jar",
+ identifier.quote = "\"")
> con <- dbConnect(drv, "jdbc:h2:~/test", "sa", "")
>
> # this works to create table with lower case names
> s <- 'create table tt("id" int primary key, "name" varchar(255))'
> dbSendUpdate(con, s)
> dbSendUpdate(con, "insert into tt values(1, 'Hello')")
> dbSendUpdate(con, "insert into tt values(2, 'World')")
> dbGetQuery(con, "select * from tt")
  id  name
1  1 Hello
2  2 World
>
> # this does not - BOD has upper case names
> dbWriteTable(con, "BOD", BOD)
[1] TRUE
> dbGetQuery(con, "select * from BOD")
  TIME DEMAND
1    1    8.3
2    2   10.3
3    3   19.0
4    4   16.0
5    5   15.6
6    7   19.8
>
> dbDisconnect(con)
[1] TRUE
>
> R.Version.string
Error: object 'R.Version.string' not found
> packageDescription("RJDBC")$Version
[1] "0.1-5"
> packageDescription("DBI")$Version
[1] "0.2-5"

