On Jan 28, 2010, at 10:55 , Tom Stockton wrote:

> Is it possible to call DataTable via .jcall() to edit a data.frame  
> in JGR. I'm not a very experienced Java programmer but I've looked  
> through the JGR source to see how this could be done, without luck.   
> I tried mimicing the calls to the JGRObjectManager (Browser) in  
> JGR.R but couldn't figure out what Method to call (this last  
> statement may really show my lack of experience).
>

The easy part - calling a DataTable:

.jnew("org.rosuda.JGR.toolkit.DataTable")

But I suspect that's not quite what you had in mind ;).

What you probably envisioned is far more complex, because in the  
ObjectBrowser it seems so easy to just click on the data frame, but  
behind the scenes a lot of things happen - the data frame is actually  
retrieved, split up and loaded into a special structure into Java and  
only then you can even think of using DataTable. I would not bother  
trying to replicate that from R not only because of the complexity but  
also that this all is JGR-internal and can change at any time.
If you still want to have a dab, you'll have to write something like a  
modified version of the RController.newSet() method and its result can  
then be fed to new DataTable call.

Cheers,
Simon

